WEBVTT

00:01.041 --> 00:02.911
Castle Arcantez

00:03.411 --> 00:06.191
A toast to our alliance

00:03.791 --> 00:07.211
<b>The Intention of the Seitz Army</b>

00:06.191 --> 00:09.921
and your ascendance to the 
governorship of Seitz Province.

00:09.921 --> 00:13.551
<b>Governor of Seitz
Grenda Domatheson</b>

00:10.231 --> 00:13.551
I'm still getting used to the title.

00:14.041 --> 00:19.561
I'm grateful you're willing to work 
with us, unlike your predecessor.

00:14.111 --> 00:17.681
<b>Vasmarque Salamakhia</b>

00:19.561 --> 00:25.211
We seek good relations with the 
future governor of Missian.

00:25.211 --> 00:27.961
Our interests are aligned.

00:27.961 --> 00:34.201
I pledge on the honor of Seitz
 to work with you.

00:34.201 --> 00:38.081
My hope is to isolate Canarre 
from the main force.

00:38.561 --> 00:42.851
Canarre has too much power 
for a single district.

00:42.851 --> 00:45.831
I want you to lock them down.

00:52.341 --> 00:54.921
My right hand, Borotz.

00:53.881 --> 00:58.091
<b>Borotz Heygand</b>

00:54.921 --> 00:57.881
He was my commander 
during the insurrection.

00:57.881 --> 01:00.351
It is an honor to meet you.

01:00.671 --> 01:03.961
He'll lead the upcoming 
invasion of Canarre, as well.

01:03.961 --> 01:07.481
We intend to send 80,000 soldiers.

01:07.481 --> 01:10.201
Impressive dedication.

01:10.201 --> 01:12.361
That's ten times Canarre's army.

01:13.031 --> 01:17.361
There's something in Canarre 
I'm quite eager to obtain.

01:18.871 --> 01:22.881
And so, in exchange for victory,
you want food, resources,

01:22.881 --> 01:27.251
and all spoils from 
the invasion of Canarre?

01:27.641 --> 01:29.751
Yes, if you please.

01:29.751 --> 01:32.991
Is it their troops you're after?

01:32.991 --> 01:34.611
I'll be going now.

01:35.561 --> 01:38.661
I'd like to begin
preparations immediately.

01:39.461 --> 01:41.261
If you don't mind, I've been curious...

01:41.771 --> 01:46.021
What do you seek to accomplish 
by becoming governor of Missian?

01:46.021 --> 01:47.521
Independence?

01:48.611 --> 01:53.031
Couran is a sad man, incapable of trust.

01:53.031 --> 01:55.781
Even if he is family.

01:56.371 --> 02:00.301
I want to protect our land 
and people as my father did.

02:00.301 --> 02:01.661
That is all.

02:02.981 --> 02:05.811
Don't worry. We'll take down Canarre.

02:05.811 --> 02:10.121
You can focus on settling accounts 
between you and your brother.

02:16.591 --> 02:20.881
Borotz, round up soldiers 
from all regions of Seitz.

02:20.881 --> 02:23.041
If I may, Governor...

02:23.041 --> 02:27.351
This conquest in Canarre
is pointless for us.

02:28.231 --> 02:32.361
It will not win us much in the 
way of territory or provisions.

02:32.361 --> 02:34.251
Especially right after the insurrection...

02:34.251 --> 02:36.021
Should you not have asked for more?

02:36.021 --> 02:37.361
Borotz.

02:37.811 --> 02:41.071
Are you aware of a man named Ars Louvent?

02:41.701 --> 02:44.251
The current headman 
of Canarre? What of him?

02:44.251 --> 02:46.631
He's but thirteen years old.

02:46.631 --> 02:49.191
Don't you find that strange?

02:49.191 --> 02:53.881
I've heard he has a curious ability 
to perceive the talents of others.

02:54.321 --> 02:56.671
Perceive their talents?

02:56.671 --> 03:01.841
I looked into it, and he <i>does</i> have a 
number of extremely talented retainers.

03:02.241 --> 03:08.391
I want to occupy Canarre and 
take Ars Louvent for myself!

03:08.391 --> 03:12.581
I also value you as my right hand.

03:12.581 --> 03:14.701
I'm counting on you.

03:18.931 --> 03:20.991
Ars Louvent...

03:21.711 --> 03:24.401
Just what kind of man is he?

04:55.041 --> 05:00.091
<b>Episode 26   Canarre in Crisis</b>

04:56.401 --> 04:59.381
I'll read the message Krall has sent us.

04:59.821 --> 05:06.621
"Seitz is mustering 80,000 soldiers 
on the border with Missian.

05:06.621 --> 05:09.391
We request urgent action."

05:09.391 --> 05:12.421
Eighty thousand? Can that really be true?

05:12.421 --> 05:14.641
That's ten times what Canarre has!

05:15.201 --> 05:20.521
If it is true, Coumeire's forces alone
 won't be enough to halt their advance.

05:20.881 --> 05:23.561
But why is Seitz being so aggressive?

05:23.561 --> 05:26.761
They had their own civil war 
not long ago, didn't they?

05:26.761 --> 05:27.571
Yes.

05:28.521 --> 05:34.131
We signed a secret peace treaty 
with Seitz during the war.

05:34.131 --> 05:41.721
But it appears the former governor's 
retainers staged a coup and overthrew him.

05:41.721 --> 05:44.431
Which means that treaty is null and void.

05:45.541 --> 05:48.001
But why now, I wonder?

05:48.001 --> 05:52.261
They're only just recovering, 
so things must be still chaotic.

05:52.261 --> 05:54.601
I don't like it.

05:55.211 --> 05:59.781
Your forces are set to rendezvous
with Couran's, right?

05:59.781 --> 06:00.481
Yes.

06:00.981 --> 06:04.531
I don't get the feeling
 Seitz is being strong-armed.

06:04.531 --> 06:06.821
Someone behind the scenes has a plan.

06:07.951 --> 06:09.661
Sorry I'm late.

06:09.661 --> 06:10.961
Pham!

06:10.961 --> 06:13.241
What did you see of Seitz's army?

06:13.901 --> 06:15.371
In a word...

06:15.801 --> 06:19.401
It's bad. I've never seen
 a camp that large.

06:19.401 --> 06:21.251
And their commander is excellent.

06:21.251 --> 06:26.691
In the insurrection, they took out 
a force of 100,000 with half that.

06:26.691 --> 06:27.631
Also...

06:28.581 --> 06:32.451
Is that a flame magistone?

06:32.451 --> 06:33.221
Don't tell me...

06:33.551 --> 06:38.541
Indeed, you can't mine flame 
magistones in Seitz.

06:38.541 --> 06:41.381
That gave me a hunch, so I looked into it,

06:41.381 --> 06:42.791
and I was right.

06:42.791 --> 06:48.491
While Seitz is marching on us, Vasmarque 
will be sending soldiers to Verzud.

06:48.491 --> 06:54.871
Sounds like Vasmarque's signed an alliance
with the new governor of Seitz.

06:55.241 --> 06:57.151
What, is that bad?

06:57.151 --> 07:00.981
Lord Couran won't be able to send aid.

07:01.721 --> 07:06.631
We'll have to fight Seitz's 80,000 troops
 with what we have on hand.

07:07.311 --> 07:10.661
H-How are Canarre's defenses?

07:10.661 --> 07:12.931
Though we'll naturally have
the advantage defending,

07:12.931 --> 07:15.761
Canarre's infrastructure isn't excellent.

07:16.811 --> 07:19.391
We can hold out... a year, I'd expect.

07:22.191 --> 07:24.981
<i>Canarre's going to fall at this rate.</i>

07:24.981 --> 07:26.401
<i>What do I do?</i>

07:27.571 --> 07:29.651
Betrayal's always an option.

07:32.651 --> 07:36.771
Obviously, if we surrender, 
the enemy will occupy Canarre.

07:36.771 --> 07:40.001
But it might at least save your life.

07:40.911 --> 07:44.051
With your Appraisal power, 
you can still make your way,

07:44.051 --> 07:46.671
which may save your retainers, as well.

07:47.861 --> 07:48.961
Unacceptable.

07:49.701 --> 07:52.281
Canarre is the land 
Lord Couran entrusted to me.

07:52.281 --> 07:54.741
I inherited it from Lord Lumeire.

07:54.741 --> 07:58.431
And most of all, this is the 
land my father protected.

07:58.931 --> 08:03.341
The reason I serve here as lord 
is to defend my homeland.

08:03.341 --> 08:06.191
It would be all too easy
 to hand this place over.

08:06.691 --> 08:10.651
But what if the enemy pillages,
ravages, and makes my people suffer?

08:11.191 --> 08:14.701
Everything I've done so far 
has been to prevent that.

08:15.201 --> 08:17.861
That is the one option I will not accept.

08:17.861 --> 08:21.701
For me and the people who have 
protected Canarre all this time...

08:22.271 --> 08:24.831
This is a battle we can't afford to lose!

08:27.171 --> 08:29.201
I thought you might say that.

08:29.781 --> 08:33.681
It looks like the enemy will 
make their move in a few weeks.

08:36.571 --> 08:39.901
Put out a meeting call 
to the lords of Canarre.

08:39.901 --> 08:43.251
In one week, we'll make 
for Coumeire Domain.

08:43.251 --> 08:44.361
Yes, sir!

08:45.241 --> 08:48.711
<i>The new House Louvent has 
only existed a few months...</i>

08:48.711 --> 08:50.911
<i>and we're already being tested!</i>

08:52.401 --> 08:55.071
One Week Later

08:54.831 --> 08:55.991
Lord Ars!

08:56.361 --> 08:58.101
Word from Lord Couran!

08:58.101 --> 08:58.991
And...

09:01.411 --> 09:03.221
<i>I understand your situation.</i>

09:03.781 --> 09:06.871
<i>The defense of Canarre 
is crucial to all of us.</i>

09:06.871 --> 09:10.241
<i>You'll be facing a harder battle 
than any you've faced before,</i>

09:10.241 --> 09:12.781
<i>but I believe you and your 
people can overcome it.</i>

09:13.861 --> 09:17.671
<i>Perhaps I'm being overprotective, 
but I've sent a few soldiers your way.</i>

09:17.671 --> 09:19.151
<i>Put them to good use.</i>

09:22.061 --> 09:25.231
Twenty thousand reinforcements 
from Lord Couran!

09:26.191 --> 09:27.441
Amazing!

09:30.711 --> 09:32.361
Clamant!

09:32.361 --> 09:34.271
The Maitraw company!

09:34.271 --> 09:36.281
What a boon they will be!

09:36.281 --> 09:40.101
But Lord Couran has his own battle 
against Lord Vasmarque to fight...

09:40.101 --> 09:41.371
Ars!

09:41.371 --> 09:44.411
Hammond Pleide, 
lord of Torbequista Domain,

09:44.411 --> 09:47.001
has come to aid Canarre
 in its hour of need!

09:47.301 --> 09:49.141
Hammond!

09:49.141 --> 09:50.131
And...

09:52.711 --> 09:54.881
I brought the boys, kiddo.

09:54.881 --> 09:59.011
They were all raring to go. 
Wouldn't stop asking.

10:00.611 --> 10:03.931
Deputy lord of Lamburg, Mireille Grangeon,

10:03.931 --> 10:06.141
has arrived to serve her lord.

10:06.611 --> 10:10.901
You're not the only one who 
thinks this battle is crucial!

10:12.631 --> 10:13.691
Yes!

10:15.831 --> 10:17.081
Everyone!

10:17.081 --> 10:18.901
I'm glad to have you!

10:29.931 --> 10:31.921
Let's hear it, Rosell.

10:32.201 --> 10:36.051
How do you take down an army of 
80,000 with a mere 28,000 troops?

10:36.051 --> 10:39.051
We don't need to take them down.

10:39.051 --> 10:41.181
What do you mean?

10:41.571 --> 10:44.271
Their forces have just come 
off a prolonged conflict.

10:44.271 --> 10:47.411
Their soldiers aren't likely 
to be at their best.

10:47.411 --> 10:51.781
Plus, this invasion is 
a conquest for them.

10:51.781 --> 10:55.821
It's not existential like 
their civil war was.

10:56.181 --> 10:58.551
In other words, their morale will be low!

10:59.741 --> 11:02.391
The only reason they would 
ally with Lord Vasmarque

11:02.391 --> 11:07.261
is because they think there's something 
to be gained by invading us.

11:07.261 --> 11:11.751
So we need to convince 
them that this isn't true.

11:12.161 --> 11:16.501
What we should focus on 
isn't beating 80,000 foes.

11:16.501 --> 11:19.331
It's using our 28,000 
troops the right way

11:19.331 --> 11:23.061
to make Seitz think they'll lose 
more than they have to gain

11:23.061 --> 11:24.641
so that they give up!

11:24.951 --> 11:29.321
For better or worse, 
this isn't a simple math equation.

11:29.321 --> 11:31.851
That's what's interesting 
about combat, right?

11:32.441 --> 11:39.141
So this isn't a fight to defeat the 
enemy, but to break their spirit!

11:39.141 --> 11:42.001
Not least of all for Couran, 
who sent us backup...

11:42.001 --> 11:44.241
Let's give this our best, everyone!

11:45.671 --> 11:47.121
Wow!

11:47.491 --> 11:49.311
It fits perfectly and everything!

11:49.311 --> 11:50.331
Yes.

11:52.361 --> 11:56.401
I won't be able to stay by your 
side during this operation.

11:56.401 --> 12:01.191
But that armor will surely 
protect you in my stead.

12:02.041 --> 12:03.321
Thank you!

12:03.321 --> 12:04.481
Lord Ars!

12:05.671 --> 12:07.811
I have something for you, as well.

12:09.031 --> 12:10.761
What are you doing, Licia?!

12:10.761 --> 12:13.911
I'm cleansing you with 
rulla leaves and petals.

12:13.911 --> 12:16.691
It's an old Torbequistan good luck ritual.

12:18.461 --> 12:23.901
They say if you then embrace the subject
like so, it guarantees their safe return.

12:24.401 --> 12:27.531
I believe the Torbequistan 
custom only requires water...

12:27.531 --> 12:29.131
R-Regardless...

12:29.671 --> 12:33.661
I'll look after Canarre in 
your absence, Lord Ars.

12:35.061 --> 12:36.271
I'll see you again soon.

12:39.691 --> 12:45.281
The battlefield will be the Coumeire 
River between Missian and Seitz.

12:45.281 --> 12:49.611
We collapsed all the bridges, 
so the enemy will likely cross here.

12:49.611 --> 12:52.561
It's where the river is narrow 
and relatively shallow.

12:53.261 --> 12:56.061
It's the only place 80,000 
soldiers could ford it.

12:56.481 --> 13:01.121
Our main force of 20,000 has already 
met up with Coumeire's army.

13:01.621 --> 13:05.651
They'll establish camp along the river 
to hold off the enemy vanguard.

13:06.071 --> 13:09.331
The rest will provide assistance 
from Coumeire Fortress,

13:09.331 --> 13:13.521
including intercepting any forces 
coming the long way around.

13:16.141 --> 13:19.791
I'll entrust command of 
the main force to you, Rietz.

13:20.751 --> 13:24.171
<b>The Night Before the Battle</b>

13:23.921 --> 13:26.791
You've done a fantastic job 
holding them off so far.

13:27.821 --> 13:30.471
Well, I know how to handle 
a defensive battle.

13:30.471 --> 13:32.141
But the real thing's soon to come.

13:32.811 --> 13:34.981
We have the terrain advantage.

13:34.981 --> 13:37.871
You've composed an 
excellent plan, as well.

13:41.211 --> 13:43.791
Tomorrow, we'll reach the Coumeire River.

13:43.791 --> 13:46.401
Everyone, rest well so 
you'll be ready for combat!

13:46.841 --> 13:50.191
There's no way I can rest 
before my first real battle.

13:50.191 --> 13:53.791
When we arrive at the battlefield, 
we'll check our equipment, and then...

13:54.761 --> 13:55.871
It's addressed to you.

13:55.871 --> 13:58.041
Th-Thank you.

14:01.421 --> 14:04.281
What made you decide 
to serve a lord?!

14:04.281 --> 14:06.431
Why would you ask that?

14:06.431 --> 14:08.011
It's not like it's a big deal.

14:08.011 --> 14:11.631
But you're a dang celebrity, man!

14:11.631 --> 14:14.971
You led the shock troops of 
the famous Riven company!

14:14.971 --> 14:17.141
I can't believe you're with us!

14:17.141 --> 14:20.151
Is there some big dream you're chasing?!

14:20.661 --> 14:22.651
Money, I guess.

14:22.931 --> 14:23.881
Money?

14:24.391 --> 14:29.221
I just thought serving a noble would 
be a good way to make money.

14:29.221 --> 14:30.781
Right...

14:30.781 --> 14:35.291
Hey, you guys! You won't get much 
sleep once the battle starts.

14:35.841 --> 14:38.621
Anyway, I'm gonna head to bed.

14:39.061 --> 14:41.231
Charlotte's amazing.

14:41.231 --> 14:43.411
It's like nothing fazes her.

14:43.411 --> 14:46.471
Charlotte's always been that way.

14:46.471 --> 14:48.781
She's made of sterner stuff than us!

14:51.781 --> 14:55.261
<i>Musia, I truly worry for you, my daughter.</i>

14:55.831 --> 14:59.301
<i>You're simply not cut out for battle.</i>

14:59.301 --> 15:02.521
<i>You're clumsy, just like I am.</i>

15:03.971 --> 15:10.011
<i>You have beautiful hair and fine features, 
so I know you could find a good husband.</i>

15:10.831 --> 15:15.351
<i>Leave the fighting to the men 
and come home. I beg you.</i>

15:20.141 --> 15:21.371
I have to sleep.

15:22.121 --> 15:25.671
<b>Fear</b>

15:29.611 --> 15:31.171
Charlotte?

15:31.521 --> 15:34.501
Oh, it's just you, Musia. You startled me.

15:34.501 --> 15:36.341
You're still awake?

15:36.341 --> 15:39.141
Just maintaining my weapon for tomorrow.

15:39.141 --> 15:41.641
I always do this stuff before a battle.

15:41.641 --> 15:45.271
I don't want messed-up gear 
holding back my true power, y'know?

15:45.271 --> 15:48.821
I'll be turning in soon, 
so make sure you do the same.

15:48.821 --> 15:50.851
Don't wanna collapse 
on your first deployment.

15:50.851 --> 15:52.091
Right...

15:54.611 --> 15:58.491
Charlotte, don't you fear battle?

15:58.921 --> 16:04.161
I... I left my village hoping 
to be useful to someone...

16:04.161 --> 16:06.831
I've worked hard in my training, too.

16:06.831 --> 16:08.891
But... I'm afraid.

16:09.781 --> 16:12.261
How can I stop feeling scared?

16:14.381 --> 16:15.721
I'm scared, too.

16:16.091 --> 16:17.261
Huh? But...

16:17.261 --> 16:21.141
Oh, I'm not afraid of dying. 
Like hell am I getting defeated.

16:22.651 --> 16:26.481
But I've spent a long time on the 
battlefield. I've killed a lot of people.

16:26.941 --> 16:30.061
I've lived a good life.
 I'd have no regrets if I fell.

16:30.061 --> 16:33.171
The thing I'm a lot more afraid of...

16:33.611 --> 16:35.741
is betraying Ars's faith in me.

16:37.701 --> 16:41.151
<i>I've always been focused on myself...</i>

16:41.151 --> 16:44.251
<i>on changing myself, 
on having more confidence...</i>

16:44.251 --> 16:46.751
<i>But she's different.</i>

16:47.101 --> 16:48.691
<i>That's why she's so strong.</i>

16:49.321 --> 16:50.251
Excuse me.

16:50.881 --> 16:53.131
Can I join you?

16:54.101 --> 16:56.511
Hell yeah. I'll teach you.

16:57.221 --> 17:01.191
<i>I hope I can be like her someday.</i>

17:04.391 --> 17:07.151
It's like he's sawing logs...

17:07.151 --> 17:10.181
You have to do something, Zaht!

17:10.181 --> 17:12.401
We'll never be able to sleep like this!

17:12.881 --> 17:15.651
Captain, you gotta quiet down—

17:17.981 --> 17:19.411
Big Bro...

17:20.241 --> 17:21.031
Dad...

17:23.781 --> 17:26.611
He's never gonna sleep soundly 
clutching that thing.

17:26.611 --> 17:28.581
I'll deal with it.

17:29.221 --> 17:30.981
We won't hear him like this.

17:30.981 --> 17:33.511
What? We totally still can!

17:33.511 --> 17:34.851
C'mon, get to bed.

17:34.851 --> 17:37.181
But those were our blankets!

17:37.181 --> 17:38.821
Yeah!

17:40.261 --> 17:44.271
Coumeire River

17:46.351 --> 17:49.021
<b>Enemy General
Lantorque Lodder</b>

17:46.351 --> 17:49.021
For Lord Borotz!

17:49.021 --> 17:52.041
Charge!

17:52.771 --> 17:54.691
We keep them from crossing.

17:54.691 --> 17:56.941
That is our mission!

17:57.871 --> 18:02.421
Bring victory to Canarre—to Lord Ars!

18:02.421 --> 18:05.121
Long-range unit at the ready!

18:05.391 --> 18:07.011
Loose arrows!

18:07.791 --> 18:09.831
Trebuchet unit, advance!

18:14.091 --> 18:16.401
Release!

18:21.201 --> 18:23.611
Magic unit, barrier spells!

18:30.441 --> 18:33.461
Vanguard, advance!

18:35.361 --> 18:37.991
Long-range unit, target their infantry!

18:44.161 --> 18:46.591
They're blocking our attacks with magic!

18:46.591 --> 18:48.791
So be it! Don't let up!

18:49.561 --> 18:51.781
Charlotte, Musia...

18:51.781 --> 18:53.541
We're counting on you.

18:54.041 --> 18:57.051
Looks like they've warmed 
things up for us.

18:57.681 --> 18:59.201
Time to get to work.

18:58.461 --> 19:01.841
<b>Musia's Determination</b>

18:59.201 --> 19:00.981
Sorry to put pressure on you,

19:00.981 --> 19:03.601
but this all comes down to us.

19:03.601 --> 19:04.721
You ready?

19:04.721 --> 19:06.161
Yes!

19:06.161 --> 19:07.061
<i>It's okay.</i>

19:07.701 --> 19:09.431
<i>My comrades' lives are riding on this.</i>

19:09.431 --> 19:11.481
<i>It'll be okay!</i>

19:11.481 --> 19:14.151
<i>I was just a normal village 
girl a few months ago...</i>

19:14.151 --> 19:15.311
<i>I can do this!</i>

19:15.311 --> 19:16.691
<i>I don't know what I can do...</i>

19:16.691 --> 19:17.691
<i>But...</i>

19:18.081 --> 19:19.861
<i>I know that I can do it!</i>

19:20.981 --> 19:22.071
Forma...

19:28.741 --> 19:30.831
I-I can't...

19:31.781 --> 19:33.831
Someone made a mistake somewhere.

19:34.111 --> 19:38.211
I've been incompetent my whole life.

19:38.731 --> 19:39.651
So I...

19:40.551 --> 19:41.501
So I...

19:44.751 --> 19:47.181
I believe in you, Musia.

19:47.581 --> 19:49.701
You have all the power you need.

19:49.701 --> 19:52.021
Ars said so, so I know it's true.

19:55.541 --> 19:56.801
Have faith.

19:59.661 --> 20:03.611
I want to be like you, Charlotte!

20:06.701 --> 20:09.081
Um, give me a knife, please!

20:10.421 --> 20:13.321
<i>I've never believed in myself before.</i>

20:13.321 --> 20:15.921
<i>But I want to believe in myself someday.</i>

20:15.921 --> 20:18.281
<i>I want to become strong enough that I can.</i>

20:18.741 --> 20:19.671
<i>So...</i>

20:27.391 --> 20:31.391
<i>For now, I'll believe in Charlotte,
 who believes in me!</i>

20:32.451 --> 20:37.361
Forma Terra Akos Magnus!

20:48.821 --> 20:49.531
What the...

20:52.661 --> 20:53.661
The water...

20:53.661 --> 20:56.041
Long-range unit, loose!

20:56.371 --> 21:00.461
Forma Igni Erupt!

21:00.461 --> 21:04.381
Now's our chance! Charge as fast as you can!

21:11.531 --> 21:13.351
All right, it's our turn!

21:13.721 --> 21:16.091
Zaht! Keep up, okay?!

21:16.091 --> 21:18.731
Don't rush too far ahead!

21:27.851 --> 21:30.201
Wh-What's going on here?

21:33.201 --> 21:37.211
R-Retreat!

21:46.741 --> 21:47.991
Nice work.

21:53.011 --> 21:54.481
Thank you!

23:26.231 --> 23:29.381
Well, Rietz? My Musia's 
pretty awesome, huh?!

23:29.381 --> 23:32.161
Indeed. And she's a nice girl, 
unlike someone I know.

23:32.161 --> 23:34.411
Hey, I'm a nice girl, too!

23:34.411 --> 23:36.831
But enough talk. 
It looks like they're up next.

23:37.141 --> 23:39.231
Next time: "Zaht and Braham."

23:37.621 --> 23:40.081
<b>Next Time   Zaht and Braham</b>
